const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文检验个券的流动性度量是否随共同市场条件而变化。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The paper tests whether individual-security liquidity measures move with common market conditions. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源把个券与市场汇总的价差、深度和交易活跃度放在同一横截面与时间序列框架中比较。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It compares security-level and market-aggregate spreads, depth, and trading activity in a joint cross-sectional and time-series framework. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要可比较的报价价差、深度、成交量、个券权重、市场汇总规则及交易日时间对齐。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Comparable quoted spreads, depth, volume, security weights, market-aggregation rules, and trading-day alignment are needed. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"研究关注流动性共同变化，而不是声称任一单一指标即可完整代表交易成本或市场承压。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The study concerns common movement in liquidity; it does not claim any single measure fully represents trading cost or market stress. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"统一报价、深度和成交字段口径，保留样本成员变动与停牌，明确市场汇总权重及异常行情处理。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Standardize quote, depth, and trade fields; retain membership changes and halts; state market weights and outlier-quote handling. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Financial Economics (2000)。不同交易制度下的价差和深度不必可比；日频代理也不能取代原文所需的报价和订单簿观察。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Financial Economics (2000). Spreads and depth can differ across trading regimes, and daily proxies cannot replace the quote and order-book observation required by the source. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0304-405x(99)00057-4",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics (2000) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Commonality in Liquidity”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。不同交易制度下的价差和深度不必可比；日频代理也不能取代原文所需的报价和订单簿观察。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Commonality in Liquidity”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
